    <string name="setup_autostart_body">Your phone closes background apps very thoroughly. With autostart, Drive Assistant may start by itself as soon as you switch on your display.\n\nTap the button below and switch on Drive Assistant in the list. If the switch already shows on: switch it off and on again.</string>
    <string name="setup_autostart_title">Allow autostart</string>
    <string name="setup_back">Back</string>
    <string name="setup_battery_action">Remove restriction</string>
    <string name="setup_battery_body">So the app stays connected while the screen is off, Android should not restrict it to save battery.\n\nThis does not use more battery: the app is only active while your display is connected.</string>
    <string name="setup_battery_body_xiaomi">So the app stays connected while the screen is off, your phone should not restrict it to save battery.\n\nTap the button below and choose No restrictions on the battery page. Then come back to the app.\n\nThis does not use more battery: the app is only active while your display is connected.</string>
    <string name="setup_battery_title">Don\'t restrict battery</string>
    <string name="setup_bt_action">Allow Bluetooth</string>
    <string name="setup_bt_body">To connect to your Drive Assistant, the app needs the Bluetooth permission (Nearby devices).\n\nThe notification permission is optional – it only shows when the display is connected.</string>
    <string name="setup_bt_title">Allow Bluetooth</string>
    <string name="setup_connect_body">Switch on your Drive Assistant now – it shows the wait screen – and tap the button. After that the app connects automatically.</string>
    <string name="setup_done_body">From now on, using your Drive Assistant is simple:\n\n1. Switch on the display\n2. Start navigation in Google Maps\n3. Ride\n\nYou don\'t need to open the app for this. You can run this setup again any time from the ⋮ menu at the top right.</string>
    <string name="setup_done_title">All set!</string>
    <string name="setup_finish">Done</string>
    <string name="setup_next">Next</string>
    <string name="setup_notif_body">Google Maps shows the turn directions in a notification. The app reads exactly that one – and the song title for the music screen. Everything else is discarded immediately.\n\nTap the button below and switch on Drive Assistant. Android shows a general warning – that is normal.</string>
    <string name="setup_notif_restricted_body">Google Maps shows the turn directions in a notification. The app reads exactly that one – and the song title. Everything else is discarded immediately.\n\nBecause the app does not come from the Play Store, Android blocks this setting at first. It takes three parts – the buttons below guide you:\n1. Try access once – Android says Restricted setting, close it with OK\n2. Allow restricted settings\n3. Switch on access</string>
    <string name="setup_notif_title">Notification access</string>
    <string name="setup_notif_try">Try access</string>
    <string name="setup_notif_try_again">Switch on notification access</string>
    <string name="setup_pair_action">Pair now</string>
    <string name="setup_pair_body">Switch on your Drive Assistant now – it shows the wait screen.\n\nThen tap Pair now and confirm the dialog. From then on your phone starts the app by itself as soon as you switch on the display.</string>
    <string name="setup_pair_title">Pair Drive Assistant</string>
